  "authorNotes": "Nursery English. No Mohammadpur 2026 final exists for Nursery, so the guide is the Mohammadpur Annual 2025 Nursery English paper (MP_OTHER / MP_OTHER_ADAPTED). Its rows match the Sylhet syllabus almost one-to-one and every word is in the 2026 Nursery English book, so most of it was reused. Changes: Q1 Mohammadpur asked A–O; the Sylhet row asks A–Z, so it is split A–I (5), J–R (5), S–Z (5). Mohammadpur had one combined 'After & Before' question with 5 + 5 items; the Sylhet paper has separate 'after' and 'before' rows of 10 each, so the 5 Mohammadpur items in each are kept and 5 new ones added (the new 'after' items use capital letters and the new 'before' items use small letters, for variety). Fill-in-the-gaps: Mohammadpur printed a capital 'J' in a small-letter grid; corrected to 'j'. Picture first-letter: Mohammadpur's sunflower picture (answer S) was replaced with a fan (F), because the book's flower picture is taught as F for flower and a 4-year-old could reasonably write F. For the picture rows the answer key accepts either the capital or the small letter. Things the owner should know: (a) The syllabus text says 'Oral 10 · Dictation 5 · Handwriting 2 are outside the 100', but the published marks table puts 'Oral 15 × 1' inside the 100. I followed the table (Oral = 15 prompts, 1 mark each, inside the 100). Please confirm which is right. (b) The syllabus lists 'Writing own name' under the written part, but there is no row for it in the marks table, so it is not in the paper (the child normally writes the name on the cover). (c) Duration 1 h 30 min is copied from the Mohammadpur paper. Page numbers in bookRef are the printed page numbers of the 2026 Nursery English book."
